\n\n### How to Get a Free .com.np Domain in Nepal\n\nThe official registrar for .np domains is **Mercantile Communication** (register.com.np). In Nepal, `.com.np` domains are **100% free of charge** for registered businesses and citizens!\n\n#### Required Documents for Business .com.np Registration:\n1. Company / Firm Registration Certificate (from Ward Office or Office of the Company Registrar).\n2. PAN / VAT Certificate.\n3. Official Application Letter on company letterhead requesting domain registration.\n\n---\n\n### DNS Configuration Steps for Sazilo Store\n\nOnce your domain is approved by Mercantile or purchased from a global registrar:\n\n1. **Log in to your DNS Management Panel** (Cloudflare, Register.com.np, or Namecheap).\n2. **Add a CNAME Record**:\n   - **Type**: `CNAME`\n   - **Host / Name**: `www`\n   - **Target / Value**: `domains.sazilostore.com`\n   - **TTL**: `Auto` or `300`\n3. **Add an A Record (for root domain)**:\n   - **Type**: `A`\n   - **Host / Name**: `@`\n   - **IP Address**: Sazilo Store Edge IP (found in your store settings dashboard).\n4. **Save and Verify**: Sazilo Store automatically verifies DNS propagation and provisions a free SSL security certificate within 15 minutes.\n\nYour branded domain is now live! [Start your store on Sazilo Store](https://sazilostore.vritico.com/register).\n\n---\n*Cover Image Credit: Photo by [NASA](https://unsplash.com/photos/Q1p7bh3SHj8) on [Unsplash](https://unsplash.com?utm_source=sazilostore&utm_medium=referral) (Royalty-free under the Unsplash License)*'),(662,'## Establishing Your Custom Brand Identity in Nepal\n\nWhen you register on **Sazilo Store**, you instantly receive a free store address: `yourstore.sazilostore.com`. While this subdomain is fully functional and secure, connecting a custom domain (like `www.yourbrand.com.np` or `www.yourbrand.com`) elevates your business credibility and enhances search engine visibility.\n\n---\n\n### How to Get a Free .com.np Domain in Nepal\n\nThe official registrar for .np domains is **Mercantile Communication** (register.com.np). In Nepal, `.com.np` domains are **100% free of charge** for registered businesses and citizens!\n\n#### Required Documents for Business .com.np Registration:\n1. Company / Firm Registration Certificate (from Ward Office or Office of the Company Registrar).\n2. PAN / VAT Certificate.\n3. Official Application Letter on company letterhead requesting domain registration.\n\n---\n\n### DNS Configuration Steps for Sazilo Store\n\nOnce your domain is approved by Mercantile or purchased from a global registrar:\n\n1. **Log in to your DNS Management Panel** (Cloudflare, Register.com.np, or Namecheap).\n2. **Add a CNAME Record**:\n   - **Type**: `CNAME`\n   - **Host / Name**: `www`\n   - **Target / Value**: `domains.sazilostore.com`\n   - **TTL**: `Auto` or `300`\n3. **Add an A Record (for root domain)**:\n   - **Type**: `A`\n   - **Host / Name**: `@`\n   - **IP Address**: Sazilo Store Edge IP (found in your store settings dashboard).\n4. **Save and Verify**: Sazilo Store automatically verifies DNS propagation and provisions a free SSL security certificate within 15 minutes.\n\nYour branded domain is now live! [Start your store on Sazilo Store](https://sazilostore.vritico.com/register).\n\n---\n*Cover Image Credit: Photo by [NASA](https://unsplash.com/photos/Q1p7bh3SHj8) on [Unsplash](https://unsplash.com?utm_source=sazilostore&utm_medium=referral) (Royalty-free under the Unsplash License)*'),(663,'## The Legal Roadmap to Starting an E-Commerce Business in Nepal\n\nOperating an online business in Nepal requires following regulatory frameworks established by the Department of Commerce, Supplies and Consumer Protection, local Ward offices, and the Inland Revenue Department (IRD).\n\nWhether you are launching a home-based boutique in Lalitpur or an electronics retail chain in Pokhara, this guide walks you through every legal requirement.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Choose Your Business Legal Structure\n\n1. **Sole Proprietorship (Ekal Swamittwo Firm)**:\n   - Best for individual founders, home bakeries, and small boutiques.\n   - Registered at the Department of Cottage and Small Industries (DCSI) or local Municipal Ward Office.\n   - Simple accounting and lower registration costs.\n2. **Private Limited Company (Pvt. Ltd.)**:\n   - Best for multi-founder startups, high-growth brands, and businesses seeking investment.\n   - Registered online via the **Office of the Company Registrar (OCR)** portal (`ocr.gov.np`).\n   - Limits personal liability and allows structured equity division.\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Ward Office & Municipal Registration\nEvery commercial entity must register at the local Ward Office (Wada Karyalaya) where the office or physical inventory warehouse is situated:\n- Submit lease/rental agreement or land ownership (Lalpurja) copy.\n- Pay local municipal business taxes (typically Rs. 2,000 to Rs. 5,000 depending on ward category).\n- Receive official Ward Business Certificate.\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: PAN / VAT Registration at Inland Revenue Department (IRD)\n1. **PAN (Permanent Account Number)**: Mandatory for all commercial enterprises.\n2. **VAT (Value Added Tax - 13%)**:\n   - Mandatory if annual sales exceed Rs. 50 Lakhs for goods or Rs. 20 Lakhs for services.\n   - Mandatory for importing goods from overseas or operating in regulated trading sectors.\n\n---\n\n### Step 4: Open a Corporate Current Bank Account\nTake your registration documents, PAN/VAT certificate, board resolution, and company stamp to any commercial bank (e.g., Nabil, Global IME, NIC Asia) to open a business account.\n\n---\n\n### Step 5: Launch Your Store on Sazilo Store\nOnce your legal details are in place, register on [Sazilo Store](https://sazilostore.vritico.com/register). Connect your corporate eSewa, Khalti, and Fonepay QR merchant accounts to start receiving payments directly to your company bank account with 0% platform commission.\n\n---\n*Cover Image Credit: Photo by [Scott Graham](https://unsplash.com/photos/5fNmWej4tAA) on [Unsplash](https://unsplash.com?utm_source=sazilostore&utm_medium=referral) (Royalty-free under the Unsplash License)*'),(664,'## The Legal Roadmap to Starting an E-Commerce Business in Nepal\n\nOperating an online business in Nepal requires following regulatory frameworks established by the Department of Commerce, Supplies and Consumer Protection, local Ward offices, and the Inland Revenue Department (IRD).\n\nWhether you are launching a home-based boutique in Lalitpur or an electronics retail chain in Pokhara, this guide walks you through every legal requirement.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Choose Your Business Legal Structure\n\n1. **Sole Proprietorship (Ekal Swamittwo Firm)**:\n   - Best for individual founders, home bakeries, and small boutiques.\n   - Registered at the Department of Cottage and Small Industries (DCSI) or local Municipal Ward Office.\n   - Simple accounting and lower registration costs.\n2. **Private Limited Company (Pvt. Ltd.)**:\n   - Best for multi-founder startups, high-growth brands, and businesses seeking investment.\n   - Registered online via the **Office of the Company Registrar (OCR)** portal (`ocr.gov.np`).\n   - Limits personal liability and allows structured equity division.\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Ward Office & Municipal Registration\nEvery commercial entity must register at the local Ward Office (Wada Karyalaya) where the office or physical inventory warehouse is situated:\n- Submit lease/rental agreement or land ownership (Lalpurja) copy.\n- Pay local municipal business taxes (typically Rs. 2,000 to Rs. 5,000 depending on ward category).\n- Receive official Ward Business Certificate.\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: PAN / VAT Registration at Inland Revenue Department (IRD)\n1. **PAN (Permanent Account Number)**: Mandatory for all commercial enterprises.\n2. **VAT (Value Added Tax - 13%)**:\n   - Mandatory if annual sales exceed Rs. 50 Lakhs for goods or Rs. 20 Lakhs for services.\n   - Mandatory for importing goods from overseas or operating in regulated trading sectors.\n\n---\n\n### Step 4: Open a Corporate Current Bank Account\nTake your registration documents, PAN/VAT certificate, board resolution, and company stamp to any commercial bank (e.g., Nabil, Global IME, NIC Asia) to open a business account.\n\n---\n\n### Step 5: Launch Your Store on Sazilo Store\nOnce your legal details are in place, register on [Sazilo Store](https://sazilostore.vritico.com/register). Connect your corporate eSewa, Khalti, and Fonepay QR merchant accounts to start receiving payments directly to your company bank account with 0% platform commission.\n\n---\n*Cover Image Credit: Photo by [Scott Graham](https://unsplash.com/photos/5fNmWej4tAA) on [Unsplash](https://unsplash.com?utm_source=sazilostore&utm_medium=referral) (Royalty-free under the Unsplash License)*'),(665,'## High-Potential E-Commerce Niches in Nepal for 2026\n\nWith increasing internet adoption and digital wallet trust, new consumer categories are booming in Nepal. Here are 10 profitable online business ideas you can start today with low capital:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Himalayan Wellness & Organic Herbals\n- **Products**: Pure Shilajit resin, Jumla organic walnuts, Ilam orthodox tea, Mustang dried apples, and raw honeycomb.\n- **Why It Works**: High local demand in Kathmandu and massive export potential to Nepali diaspora overseas.\n\n### 2. Curated Vintage & Upcycled Fashion (Thrifting)\n- **Products**: Handpicked vintage denim, oversized streetwear, reworked jackets, and retro sunglasses.\n- **Target Market**: Gen Z and university students looking for unique fashion at accessible prices.\n\n### 3. Artisanal Natural Skincare & Handmade Soaps\n- **Products**: Chiuri butter moisturizers, yak milk soaps, herbal hair oils, and clay face masks.\n- **Why It Works**: Consumers are actively avoiding chemical-laden imports in favor of gentle, locally sourced botanicals.\n\n### 4. Custom Jewelry & Handcrafted Silver Accessories\n- **Products**: Minimalist silver rings, brass ear cuffs, custom name pendants, and authentic bead bracelets.\n\n### 5. Specialized Pet Care Supplies & Gourmet Treats\n- **Products**: Hypoallergenic dog treats, organic catnip, chew toys, and personalized dog collars.\n\n### 6. Traditional Handloom Dhaka & Contemporary Apparel\n- **Products**: Dhaka blazers, modern ties, pocket squares, laptop sleeves, and tote bags made from authentic Palpali and Terhathumi Dhaka.\n\n### 7. Mobile Gaming & Content Creator Accessories\n- **Products**: Clip-on phone cooling fans, ring lights, lavalier microphones, phone gaming triggers, and studio backdrops.\n\n### 8. Gourmet Bakery, Cloud Treats & Artisanal Chocolates\n- **Products**: Basque burnt cheesecakes, sourdough loaves, customized birthday hampers, and handcrafted chocolate truffles.\n\n### 9. Indoor Plants, Ceramic Pots & Balcony Gardening Kits\n- **Products**: Air-purifying succulents, Bhaktapur ceramic planters, cocopeat bricks, and indoor plant fertilizer sprays.\n\n### 10. Educational Toys, STEM Kits & Children\'s Books\n- **Products**: Wooden Montessori puzzles, interactive Nepali alphabet flashcards, and hands-on science experiments.\n\n---\n\n### Comparison of Starting Costs and Profit Margins\n\n| Business Idea | Initial Capital Needed | Average Gross Margin | Sazilo Store Theme Fit |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Himalayan Wellness | Rs. 25,000 – Rs. 60,000 | 45% – 65% | Organic & Gourmet Food |\n| Vintage Streetwear | Rs. 15,000 – Rs. 35,000 | 50% – 70% | Modern Fashion & Apparel |\n| Artisanal Skincare | Rs. 20,000 – Rs. 50,000 | 55% – 75% | Beauty & Cosmetics |\n| Handmade Jewelry | Rs. 30,000 – Rs. 80,000 | 40% – 60% | Luxury & Jewelry |\n| Cloud Bakery Hamper | Rs. 10,000 – Rs. 25,000 | 50% – 60% | Food & Bakery |\n\nTurn your idea into reality today. [Create your free store on Sazilo Store](https://sazilostore.vritico.com/register).\n\n---\n*Cover Image Credit: Photo by [Brooke Cagle](https://unsplash