pal\'s Roads\n\nNepal\'s diverse geography presents unique logistics hurdles: monsoon rains, bumpy highway roads, and frequent parcel transfers between cargo trucks and local delivery bikes.\n\nPackaging fragile goods properly ensures they arrive in pristine condition, reducing return disputes and negative customer reviews.\n\n---\n\n### Packaging Best Practices by Category\n\n#### 1. Glass, Ceramics & Pottery (Bhaktapur Crafts, Perfumes)\n- Wrap items individually in **2 to 3 layers of high-density air bubble wrap**.\n- Use corrugated 5-ply cardboard outer boxes with foam corner edge protectors.\n- Affix high-visibility red **\'FRAGILE - HANDLE WITH CARE\'** stickers on all four sides of the box.\n\n#### 2. Fashion, Dhaka Apparel & Textiles\n- Use waterproof plastic poly mailers with tamper-evident self-adhesive sealing strips.\n- Insert a moisture-absorbing silica gel sachet inside the inner bag during monsoon months.\n\n#### 3. Electronics & Mobile Accessories\n- Place devices in anti-static protective bags before boxing.\n- Fill all empty box cavities with crushed kraft paper or air cushions to prevent movement during transit.\n\nEnhance your unboxing experience with [Sazilo Store](https://sazilostore.vritico.com/register).\n\n---\n*Cover Image Credit: Photo by [Raimond Klavins](https://unsplash.com/photos/u4g7F7e2lZQ) on [Unsplash](https://unsplash.com?utm_source=sazilostore&utm_medium=referral) (Royalty-free under the Unsplash License)*'),(696,'## Protecting Your Shipments Across Nepal\'s Roads\n\nNepal\'s diverse geography presents unique logistics hurdles: monsoon rains, bumpy highway roads, and frequent parcel transfers between cargo trucks and local delivery bikes.\n\nPackaging fragile goods properly ensures they arrive in pristine condition, reducing return disputes and negative customer reviews.\n\n---\n\n### Packaging Best Practices by Category\n\n#### 1. Glass, Ceramics & Pottery (Bhaktapur Crafts, Perfumes)\n- Wrap items individually in **2 to 3 layer