 [Start using Sazilo Store POS](https://sazilostore.vritico.com/register).\n\n---\n*Cover Image Credit: Photo by [Christiann Koepke](https://unsplash.com/photos/4W4WvOgT_3c) on [Unsplash](https://unsplash.com?utm_source=sazilostore&utm_medium=referral) (Royalty-free under the Unsplash License)*'),(713,'## Scaling Beyond a Single Store Location in Nepal\n\nAs your retail brand expands from its flagship store in New Road to additional branches in Pokhara Lakeside, Butwal, and Lalitpur, maintaining control over inventory and staff becomes a major challenge.\n\nWithout a centralized cloud system, stock disappears, branch managers give unauthorized discounts, and owners spend hours making manual phone calls to check daily cash registers.\n\n---\n\n### Core Multi-Branch Management Features in Sazilo Store\n\n#### 1. Centralized Multi-Location Inventory\nView live stock levels across all your physical branches and central warehouse on a single screen. If a customer in your Pokhara showroom wants a jacket size that is sold out locally, your staff can immediately check stock at the Kathmandu warehouse and arrange express delivery.\n\n#### 2. Inter-Branch Stock Transfers (STOs)\nCreate and track structured Stock Transfer Orders:\n- New Road Branch dispatches 50 pieces.\n- Pokhara Branch scans and accepts the incoming shipment.\n- Any transit shrinkage or discrepancy is flagged automatically.\n\n#### 3. Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) & Shift Closing\nAssign distinct permission levels:\n- **Cashier**: Can only scan items, apply authorized discounts, and print bills.\n- **Branch Manager**: Can initiate restock requests and view daily branch sales.\n- **Store Owner / Admin**: Has full visibility into purchase costs, profit margins, and consolidated tax analytics across all branches.\n\nEmpower your multi-branch operations with [Sazilo Store](https://sazilostore.vritico.com/register).\n\n---\n*Cover Image Credit: Photo by [Manuel Geissinger](https://unsplash.com/photos/7kEpUPB8vNk) on [Unsplash](https://unsplash.com?utm_source=sazilostore&utm_medium=referral) (Royalty-free under the Unsplash License)*'),(714,'## Scaling Beyond a Single Store Location in Nepal\n\nAs your retail brand expands from its flagship store in New Road to additional branches in Pokhara Lakeside, Butwal, and Lalitpur, maintaining control over inventory and staff becomes a major challenge.\n\nWithout a centralized cloud system, stock disappears, branch managers give unauthorized discounts, and owners spend hours making manual phone calls to check daily cash registers.\n\n---\n\n### Core Multi-Branch Management Features in Sazilo Store\n\n#### 1. Centralized Multi-Location Inventory\nView live stock levels across all your physical branches and central warehouse on a single screen. If a customer in your Pokhara showroom wants a jacket size that is sold out locally, your staff can immediately check stock at the Kathmandu warehouse and arrange express delivery.\n\n#### 2. Inter-Branch Stock Transfers (STOs)\nCreate and track structured Stock Transfer Orders:\n- New Road Branch dispatches 50 pieces.\n- Pokhara Branch scans and accepts the incoming shipment.\n- Any transit shrinkage or discrepancy is flagged automatically.\n\n#### 3. Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) & Shift Closing\nAssign distinct permission levels:\n- **Cashier**: Can only scan items, apply authorized discounts, and print bills.\n- **Branch Manager**: Can initiate restock requests and view daily branch sales.\n- **Store Owner / Admin**: Has full visibility into purchase costs, profit margins, and consolidated tax analytics across all branches.\n\nEmpower your multi-branch operations with [Sazilo Store](https://sazilostore.vritico.com/register).\n\n---\n*Cover Image Credit: Photo by [Manuel Geissinger](https://unsplash.com/photos/7kEpUPB8vNk) on [Unsplash](https://unsplash.com?utm_source=sazilostore&utm_medium=referral) (Royalty-free under the Unsplash License)*'),(715,'## Why Professional Barcoding Is Essential for Modern Retail\n\nMany small retail shops in Nepal rely on handwritten paper price tags stuck on garments or boxes with tape. Over time, tags fall off, prices get smudged, or dishonest customers swap price tags.\n\nUsing standardized barcodes eliminates human error and makes store operations professional and tamper-proof.\n\n---\n\n### Features of Sazilo Store Barcode Studio\n\n- **Universal Code128 Format**: Industry-standard high-density barcode encoding readable by any standard 1D or 2D laser scanner.\n- **Custom Sticker Layouts**: Print on continuous thermal rolls (e.g., 50x25mm, 38x25mm) or standard 24-up / 48-up A4 adhesive sticker sheets using any normal office laser/inkjet printer!\n- **Rich Label Content**: Customize what appears on each barcode sticker:\n  - Business / Store Name (e.g., *Nepal Threads*)\n  - Product Name & Variant (e.g., *Silk Kurti - Maroon / M*)\n  - SKU Code (e.g., *NT-KURTI-MAR-M*)\n  - MRP Price in NPR (e.g., *MRP: Rs. 2,450*)\n\n---\n\n### Step-by-Step Barcode Printing Workflow\n\n1. In Sazilo Store, navigate to **Products > Barcode Studio**.\n2. Select the products or incoming shipment batch you want to label.\n3. Choose your label dimensions (Thermal Roll or A4 Sheet Grid).\n4. Click **Print Labels**. Peel and stick stickers onto your products.\n\nStart printing barcodes today with [Sazilo Store](https://sazilostore.vritico.com/register).\n\n---\n*Cover Image Credit: Photo by [Christiann Koepke](https://unsplash.com/photos/4W4WvOgT_3c) on [Unsplash](https://unsplash.com?utm_source=sazilostore&utm_medium=referral) (Royalty-free under the Unsplash License)*'),(716,'## Why Professional Barcoding Is Essential for Modern Retail\n\nMany small retail shops in Nepal rely on handwritten paper price tags stuck on garments or boxes with tape. Over time, tags fall off, prices get smudged, or dishonest customers swap price tags.\n\nUsing standardized barcodes eliminates human error and makes store operations professional and tamper-proof.\n\n---\n\n### Features of Sazilo Store Barcode Studio\n\n- **Universal Code128 Format**: Industry-standard high-density barcode encoding readable by any standard 1D or 2D laser scanner.\n- **Custom Sticker Layouts**: Print on continuous thermal rolls (e.g., 50x25mm, 38x25mm) or standard 24-up / 48-up A4 adhesive sticker sheets using any normal office laser/inkjet printer!\n- **Rich Label Content**: Customize what appears on each barcode sticker:\n  - Business / Store Name (e.g., *Nepal Threads*)\n  - Product Name & Variant (e.g., *Silk Kurti - Maroon / M*)\n  - SKU Code (e.g., *NT-KURTI-MAR-M*)\n  - MRP Price in NPR (e.g., *MRP: Rs. 2,450*)\n\n---\n\n### Step-by-Step Barcode Printing Workflow\n\n1. In Sazilo Store, navigate to **Products > Barcode Studio**.\n2. Select the products or incoming shipment batch you want to label.\n3. Choose your label dimensions (Thermal Roll or A4 Sheet Grid).\n4. Click **Print Labels**. Peel and stick stickers onto your products.\n\nStart printing barcodes today with [Sazilo Store](https://sazilostore.vritico.com/register).\n\n---\n*Cover Image Credit: Photo by [Christiann Koepke](https://unsplash.com/photos/4W4WvOgT_3c) on [Unsplash](https://unsplash.com?utm_source=sazilostore&utm_medium=referral) (Royalty-free under the Unsplash License)*'),(717,'## The Danger of Desynchronized Inventory\n\nFor retailers who operate both a physical retail counter and an active online storefront or Instagram shop, managing inventory in separate systems is a recipe for disaster:\n\n- A customer walks into your New Road shop and buys the last size \'Large\' black winter coat.\n- Ten minutes later, an online customer in Pokhara orders the exact same size \'Large\' coat on your website.\n- Your warehouse discovers the coat is out of stock, leading to an awkward phone call, a cancelled order, and a disappointed buyer.\n\n---\n\n### How Sazilo Store Delivers True Omnichannel Sync\n\n```\n                  [ UNIFIED INVENTORY DATABASE ]\n                                |\n               +----------------+----------------+\n               |                                 |\n     [ Physical Counter POS ]           [ Online Web Storefront ]\n  Cashier scans barcode in New Road   Customer adds to cart & checks out\n               |                                 |\n               +-------> Stock count -1 <--------+\n                     (Synchronized <15ms)\n```\n\n1. **Atomic Stock Decrement**: The moment a barcode is scanned at the physical counter or an online checkout completes, inventory is decremented instantly across all channels.\n2. **Low Stock Threshold Alerts**: Set automated notifications when stock drops below 5 units so your purchasing team can reorder in advance.\n3. **Variant-Level Tracking**: Track stock down to the exact size, color, material, and storage combination.\n\nMaintain 100% accurate inventory with [Sazilo Store](https://sazilostore.vritico.com/register).\n\n---\n*Cover Image Credit: Photo by [Christiann Koepke](https://unsplash.com/photos/4W4WvOgT_3c) on [Unsplash](https://unsplash.com?utm_source=sazilostore&utm_medium=referral) (Royalty-free under the Unsplash License)*'),(718,'## The Danger of Desynchronized Inventory\n\nFor retailers who operate both a physical retail counter and an active online storefront or Instagram shop, managing inventory in separate systems is a recipe for disaster:\n\n- A customer walks into your New Road shop and buys the last size \'Large\' black winter coat.\n- Ten minutes later, an online customer in Pokhara orders the exact same size \'Large\' coat on your website.\n- Your warehouse discovers the coat is out of stock, leading to an awkward phone call, a cancelled order, and a disappointed buyer.\n\n---\n\n### How Sazilo Store Delivers True Omnichannel Sync\n\n```\n                  [ UNIFIED INVENTORY DATABASE ]\n                                |\n               +----------------+----------------+\n               |                                 |\n     [ Physical Counter POS ]           [ Online Web Storefront ]\n  Cashier scans barcode in New Road   Customer adds to cart & checks out\n               |                                 |\n               +-------> Stock count -1 <--------+\n                     (Synchronized <15ms)\n```\n\n1. **Atomic Stock Decrement**: The moment a barcode is scanned at the physical counter or an online checkout completes, inventory is decremented instantly across all channels.\n2. **Low Stock Threshold Alerts**: Set automated notifications when stock drops below 5 units so your purchasing team can reorder in advance.\n3. **Variant-Level Tracking**: Track stock down to the exact size, color, material, and storage combination.\n\nMaintain 100% accurate inventory with [Sazilo Store](https://sazilostore.vritico.com/register).\n\n---\n*Cover Image Credit: Photo by [Christiann Koepke](https://unsplash.com/photos/4W4WvOgT_3c) on [Unsplash](https://unsplash.com?utm_source=sazilostore&utm_medium=referral) (Royalty-free under the Unsplash License)*'),(719,'## Fast Queues Lead to Higher Retail Sales\n\nDuring peak festival shopping seasons like Dashain, Tihar, and Teej, long retail checkout lines cause frustrated shoppers to abandon full shopping carts.\n\nSazilo Store Cloud POS was built with high-velocity keyboard shortcuts so cashiers can ring up customers without touching a trackpad or mouse.\n\n---\n\n### Sazilo Store POS Hotkey Cheatsheet\n\n- **`F2` - Quick Search**: Instant modal to search items by product name, SKU, or category.\n- **`F4` - Cart Discount**: Apply flat discount or percentage discount to the entire order.\n- **`F7` - Hold Order**: Temporarily park a cart if a customer forgot their wallet, allowing the cashier to serve the next customer in line immediately.\n- **`F8` - Retrieve Parked Order**: Resume a held cart with a single keystroke.\n- **`F9` - Fast Checkout & Auto-Print**: Complete payment and trigger thermal slip printing in 1 click.\n- **`ESC` - Cancel / Clear**