**Jumla Organic Fuji Apples** | Jumla (Karnali) | 30–45 days (Cool Storage) | Ventilated corrugated cartons with individual foam net sleeves |\n| **Mustang Thin-Shell Walnuts** | Mustang | 6–12 months | Vacuum-sealed biodegradable stand-up kraft pouches |\n| **Jumla Black Beans (Simi)** | Jumla | 12+ months | Moisture-barrier 1kg & 5kg cotton canvas sacks |\n| **Ilam Premium Orthodox Tea** | Ilam | 18–24 months | Multi-layer nitrogen-flushed aluminum foil zipper bags |\n| **Mustang Buckwheat (Phapar)** | Mustang | 6–9 months | Food-grade airtight sealed poly pouches |\n\n---\n\n### Managing Perishable Inventory on Sazilo Store\n\n1. **Pre-Order and Harvest Batches**: Open pre-orders on your **Sazilo Store** before harvesting. When the truck leaves Jumla or Mustang, dispatch notifications automatically update waiting customers in Kathmandu.\n2. **Weight-Based Variable Units**: Configure listings by grams, kilograms, and bulk crates with automatic tier discounts (e.g., 5kg box with 10% discount).\n3. **Same-Day Valley Delivery**: Coordinate early morning central hub dispatch for fresh produce to arrive at customer doorsteps before lunch.\n\nEmpower your agro-enterprise today with [Sazilo Store](https://sazilostore.vritico.com/register).\n\n---\n*Cover Image Credit: Photo by [Markus Spiske](https://unsplash.com/photos/G3s4d_r7Pno) on [Unsplash](https://unsplash.com?utm_source=sazilostore&utm_medium=referral) (Royalty-free under the Unsplash License)*'),(808,'## The Growing Demand for Farm-to-Table Organic Groceries in Nepal\n\nHealth-conscious urban households across Kathmandu Valley and Pokhara are actively seeking verified organic vegetables, unpolished indigenous grains, Marpha dried fruits, high-altitude Jumla apples, and wild Mustang walnuts. \n\nHistorically, farmers in remote mountain districts received barely NPR 30 to NPR 50 per kilogram from intermediaries, while final retail consumers in Kathmandu paid upwards of NPR 250 per kg. Direct-to-consumer e-commerce