ed international acclaim for its delicate floral aroma, citrus acidity, and smooth chocolate undertones.\n\nPassionate coffee roasters in Kathmandu, Patan, and Pokhara are bypassing export brokers to sell fresh-roasted beans, nitro-flushed pour-over drip bags, and manual brewing equipment directly to consumers.\n\n---\n\n### Specialty Coffee Flavor Profile Matrix\n\n| Plantation Region | Elevation | Processing Method | Flavor Notes | Optimal Brew Method |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Nuwakot Mountain Valley** | 1,400m – 1,600m | Washed (Wet Process) | Jasmine, Green Apple, Honey | V60 Pour-over & Aeropress |\n| **Kavrepalanchok Highlands** | 1,300m – 1,500m | Natural (Sun-Dried) | Wild Berry, Dark Chocolate, Brown Sugar | French Press & Cold Brew |\n| **Gulmi Historic Estate** | 1,200m – 1,400m | Honey Process | Caramel, Orange Zest, Roasted Almond | Espresso Machine & Moka Pot |\n\n---\n\n### Essential Roastery Features on Sazilo Store\n\n1. **Custom Grind Size Selector**: Allow customers to choose their preferred grind at checkout:\n   - *Whole Bean* (Preserve freshness)\n   - *Coarse* (French Press / Cold Brew)\n   - *Medium* (V60 / Drip Machine / Aeropress)\n   - *Fine* (Espresso / Moka Pot)\n2. **Roast Date Transparency**: Print the exact batch roast date on every bag with a one-way degassing valve.\n3. **Monthly Coffee Bean Subscriptions**: Provide automated recurring deliveries so coffee lovers never wake up to an empty hopper.\n\nLaunch your artisanal coffee storefront on [Sazilo Store](https://sazilostore.vritico.com/register).\n\n---\n*Cover Image Credit: Photo by [Nathan Dumlao](https://unsplash.com/photos/G3s4d_r7Pno) on [Unsplash](https://unsplash.com?utm_source=sazilostore&utm_medium=referral) (Royalty-free under the Unsplash License)*'),(844,'## The Rise of Nepali Specialty Himalayan Arabica Coffee\n\nGrown at elevations between 1,200 to 1,800 meters in shade-grown mountain plantations across Nuwakot, Kavrepalanchok, Gulmi, and Sindhupal